{
    "$comment": [
        "Merge these keys into the plugin's composer.json; this file is not a composer.json of its own.",
        "Use this template when Pest cannot run (supported PHP floor below 8.2). Versions are current as of 2026-10-02 (repo.packagist.org).",
        "phpunit/phpunit ^9.6 is the PHPUnit major for a floor below PHP 8.2: PHPUnit 10 needs PHP 8.1+, and yoast/phpunit-polyfills 4.x supports PHPUnit 7.5 to 9, 11 and 12, not 10. When the floor reaches 8.2, move to the Pest templates (or PHPUnit 11) per the tests skill.",
        "Do not pin config.platform.php to the supported floor. Tooling resolves on the developer's PHP; the floor belongs in require.php (and in phpunit.xml's coverage shape for this major). Same rule as the code-quality skill. Keep an existing platform pin only when the repository already needs one for another reason.",
        "wp-phpunit/wp-phpunit follows WordPress' own versions. Pin it to the minor the installs run (wp core version), so the test library matches the core it boots.",
        "A plugin with no composer.json gets one holding these keys plus name, description, type and license, and a require block holding only php (the supported floor, which Rector and PHPStan read): development dependencies only, so nothing is installed into production."
    ],
    "require-dev": {
        "brain/monkey": "^2.7",
        "phpunit/phpunit": "^9.6",
        "wp-phpunit/wp-phpunit": "~7.1.0",
        "yoast/phpunit-polyfills": "^4.0"
    },
    "config": {
        "sort-packages": true
    },
    "scripts": {
        "test": [
            "@test:unit",
            "@test:integration"
        ],
        "test:unit": "phpunit --testsuite=Unit",
        "test:integration": "phpunit --testsuite=Integration"
    },
    "scripts-descriptions": {
        "test": "Run both suites, each in its own process, so the Unit suite never sees WordPress.",
        "test:unit": "Run the suite that needs no WordPress and no database.",
        "test:integration": "Run the suite that boots WordPress through wp-phpunit against the test database."
    }
}
